Perfect! I now have comprehensive documentation. Let me provide you with a thorough summary of all the key Next.js App Router patterns and APIs you need to know:

## Comprehensive Next.js App Router Documentation Summary

### 1. App Directory Structure & Basic Setup

The App Router uses **file-system based routing** where folders define routes and special files create UI:

**Root Layout (required)**
```tsx
// app/layout.tsx - Must contain <html> and <body> tags
export default function RootLayout({
  children,
}: {
  children: React.ReactNode
}) {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <body>{children}</body>
    </html>
  )
}
```

**Page Components**
```tsx
// app/page.tsx - Creates the home page at /
export default function Page() {
  return <h1>Hello Next.js!</h1>
}

// app/blog/page.tsx - Creates a page at /blog
export default function Page() {
  return <h1>Blog</h1>
}
```

**Nested Layouts**
```tsx
// app/blog/layout.tsx - Layout for all /blog/* routes
export default function BlogLayout({
  children,
}: {
  children: React.ReactNode
}) {
  return <section>{children}</section>
}
