### 9. Migration Path: Pages → App Router

**Key Mapping:**

| Pages Router | App Router | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `pages/_app.js` | `app/layout.tsx` | Root layout (single file) |
| `pages/_document.js` | `app/layout.tsx` | Merge with root layout |
| `pages/[slug].js` | `app/[slug]/page.tsx` | Dynamic routes still work |
| `pages/api/posts.js` | `app/api/posts/route.ts` | Route Handlers |
| `getStaticProps` | Async Server Component | Fetch directly in component |
| `getStaticPaths` | `generateStaticParams()` | Same purpose, simpler API |
| `getServerSideProps` | Async Server Component | Fetch directly in component |
| `next/head` | `generateMetadata()` or `metadata` export | Built-in SEO support |
| `pages/404.js` | `app/[...slug]/not-found.tsx` | Not found boundary |
| `pages/_error.js` | `app/error.tsx` | Error boundaries |

**Incremental Migration Strategy:**
1. Create `app/layout.tsx` (root layout)
2. Migrate pages one by one from `pages/` to `app/`
3. Move API routes to `app/api/route.ts`
4. Replace data fetching functions
5. Delete `pages/` directory when complete

